course: dictionary
lesson: 1811
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Club is a word with more than one meaning. The words around it, its context, show you which meaning is used. «Good sports clubs, like boxing or judo clubs, have strict rules against fighting outside the club.» Here the clues are sports, rules and members, so a club is a group of people who meet to do something they like.
explain: Other meanings of club are very different. A club can be a heavy stick used to hit something, or a golf club used to hit a golf ball. In a pack of cards, clubs is one of the four suits, with a black clover shape.
explain: Club can also be a verb. To club together means to put money together to buy something. When you meet a word with several meanings, try each one in the sentence and see which one still makes sense.
fact: A club is a group of people who meet to do something they like, such as reading, chess or a sport.
fact: A club can also be a heavy stick used to hit, or a golf club used to hit a golf ball.
fact: Clubs is one of the four suits in a pack of cards, with a black clover shape.
fact: To club together means to put money together to buy something.
fact: In maths, a club is a group whose members are counted, and the count changes when someone joins or leaves.
exercise: «Good sports clubs, like boxing or judo clubs, have strict rules against fighting outside the club.» What is a club in this sentence? | A golf ball | A heavy stick used to hit | *A group of people who meet to do a sport or activity together | A suit in a pack of cards
exercise: In «Wee Callum in Glasgow said he'd scored a hat-trick, and Dad was so chuffed (pleased) that the story reached the club newsletter», what is the club newsletter? | A bill for the club fees | A golf course | A game of cards | *A news sheet for the members of a club
exercise: What shape is shown on the suit of clubs in a pack of cards? | A red diamond | A black triangle | A red heart | *A black clover shape
test: Club together means... | To leave a group of friends | To win a card game | *To put money together to buy something | To hit a ball hard with a stick
test: «Before the car, Toad tries a horse-drawn caravan holiday, which was also a new fashion: the first caravan club in Britain was started the year before the book came out.» In this sentence, what is a caravan club? | *A group of people who meet because they share an interest in caravans | A holiday in the countryside | A caravan with a horse | A new kind of car
exam: In maths, a club has 10 members and 3 new children join it. How many members does the club have now? | 3 | 30 | 7 | *13
